.TH mbm_phins2fnv 1 "7 September 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbm_phins2fnv\fP \- Macro to translate processed Phins INS navigation data
to an fnv file for use in MB-System processing.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbm_phins2fnv\fP \fB\-i\fP\fIinputfile\fP \fB\-o\fP\fIoutputfile\fP
[\fB\-v\fP \fB\-h\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbm_phins2fnv\fP is a macro intended to translate processed navigation
data from an iXblue Phins inertial navigation system (INS) into an "fnv"
format navigation file of the kind used elsewhere in \fBMB-System\fP
processing (see, e.g., the \fB\-N\fP option of \fBmbnavlist\fP and the
merge-navigation options of \fBmbprocess\fP).

In the current version of this macro, the input file (specified with
\fB\-i\fP/\fB\-\-input\fP) is read using whitespace as a field delimiter, with
lines beginning with a "#" character treated as comments, and the
resulting table of columns is printed to the shell. The subsequent step
of selecting the columns needed for an fnv file and writing the file named
with \fB\-o\fP/\fB\-\-output\fP has not yet been implemented in this version of the
macro; running it currently reports the parsed input data rather than
producing an fnv output file.

Both an input and an output filename must be supplied on the command line;
if either is missing the macro prints a diagnostic message and exits
without processing.

